            "turn": 2,
            "text": "*Sets the brush down and inclines his head slightly.* I shall try this foreign tongue, though it sits strangely upon my tongue. You are Seoyun, then — a name I had not heard before today. Speak on, and I shall answer as best I can."
          },
          {
            "turn": 3,
            "text": "*Nods slowly, setting the brush aside with care.* I understand now — you cannot read our Korean letters, so I shall keep to this English tongue. It is clumsy in my mouth, but I would not have a guest strain to make himself understood. Let us speak plainly, then, and I shall hear what brings you to Gyeongbokgung."
          },
          {
            "turn": 4,
            "text": "*Frowns slightly and taps the edge of the desk.* \"Week-end,\" you say — a word I do not know, though I take it to mean the days when the court's business pauses. In such hours I most enjoy reading beside the scholars of Jiphyeonjeon, and sometimes I step out to see the water clock and the sundial that Jang Yeongsil and I made. Tell me, do your people set aside such days by the turning of the moon, or by some fixed count?"
          }
        ]
